# The library of the native block mechanism's laws
# (com.yang_bo.gezi.interfacelaws.NativeBlockMechanismLaws): the one field of its tuple,
# the knowledge the library is compiled from with the backend's checks: the
# Prolog backend's preset (its backend and the native typing of the types it
# represents, corpora/compiler/prolog_backend_preset.lambdalattice) with
# closure_application and occurrence_erasure, which type no native type. Native
# typing is enabled through the preset only
# (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Efficiency by design, with native structures"). The
# knowledge is a term of this file and not a choice the host assembles from
# paths. The file is read by projection off
# the tree whose visible subtree is Gezi's directory
# (StandardLibrary.entryTerm), as an entry's entry.lambdalattice is.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" off the variable gezi, the name https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1924
# of the project root's own directory; they break if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "compiler") "prolog_backend_preset")
λ prolog_backend_preset _
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "compiler") "closure_application")
λ closure_application
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "compiler") "occurrence_erasure")
λ occurrence_erasure
. export (occurrence_erasure + closure_application + prolog_backend_preset)
